Business Requirements Document (BRD): Enterprise SOW Reviewer MVP
1. Executive Summary & Problem Statement
Manual review of Statements of Work (SOWs) by Delivery Leads and Commercial teams is slow, inconsistent, and prone to human oversight. Missing sections—such as undefined Acceptance Criteria, omitted Roles & Responsibilities (RACI), or open-ended commitments like "unlimited revisions"—lead to severe scope creep, unbilled effort, and delivery disputes.

Objective: Build an automated SOW Reviewer MVP that ingests draft SOW documents (.pdf, .docx, .md), audits them against versioned company governance policies, flags missing sections and vague/risky clauses with verbatim evidence, computes a deterministic compliance score, and exports an actionable review report.

2. Scope & Phasing
In-Scope (MVP):

Single-document SOW upload via a lightweight Streamlit UI.

Multi-format document parsing (.pdf, .docx, .md) using Docling.

Offline knowledge preparation converting company policy and gold-standard SOW rules into token-efficient TOON (Token-Oriented Object Notation) files.

Three specialized LLM audit agents (Completeness, Risk + Vagueness, Summary) enforcing strict JSON Schema outputs.

Deterministic Python Quote Verifier and Score Engine (no LLM-based math).

Report generation (UI dashboard + downloadable Excel .xlsx and Markdown .md reports) and local SQLite History DB logging.

Out-of-Scope (Deferred to Phase 2):

Live incremental folder indexing via CocoIndex and vector database storage (pgvector).

Parent Master Services Agreement (MSA) cross-referencing.

Asynchronous worker queues (Celery/FastAPI) and SSO/RBAC authentication.

3. System Architecture & Data Flow
Part A: Knowledge Preparation (Offline / One-Time Setup)
Source Docs: Ingest company_sow_policy.md and correct_sow_sample.md (alongside .pdf/.docx equivalents).

Docling Parse: Extract normalized Markdown text and structured tables.

Checklist Compilation (knowledge/checklist_v1.toon): Store mandatory rules, severity weights, and prohibited ambiguous phrases in TOON format ([N]{fields}: tabular blocks) to reduce prompt input tokens by ~40% compared to JSON.

Part B: SOW Review Pipeline (Runtime Execution)
Streamlit UI: User uploads a draft SOW (.pdf, .docx, or .md) and clicks Run SOW Review.

Docling Parse & Sectioning: Convert uploaded file to clean Markdown preserving pipe tables (| col | col |). Split into sections by # / ## headings (with a full-document fallback flag if fewer than 3 headings are detected).

Parallel / Sequential LLM Agents (Input: TOON Rules + Parsed SOW | Output: Strict JSON):

Agent 1 — Completeness Agent: Checks SOW against mandatory policy sections (Scope, Deliverables Table, Acceptance Criteria & Sign-off Window, RACI, Payment Milestones, Assumptions, Change Control). Outputs missing or incomplete sections.

Agent 2 — Risk + Vagueness Agent: Scans SOW text for prohibited open-ended phrases (e.g., "to client's full satisfaction", "unlimited revisions", "best efforts", "TBD" milestones) and pulls exact verbatim quotes.

Agent 3 — Summary Agent: Deduplicates and merges findings from Agents 1 and 2 into a unified executive summary and prioritized remediation list.

Deterministic Guardrails & Score Engine (Pure Python — No LLM):

Quote Verifier: Checks every LLM-extracted quote against the Docling Markdown output (exact/normalized substring match). Flags unverified quotes so hallucinated citations never reach the final report.

Score Engine: Starts at 100 points and deducts deterministic penalties based on verified findings:

CRITICAL: -20 pts per finding (e.g., missing Acceptance Criteria, missing RACI, missing Payment Terms, uncapped revisions).

HIGH: -10 pts per finding (e.g., missing Out-of-Scope, missing Change Control, vague ongoing maintenance).

MEDIUM: -5 pts per finding (e.g., missing Client Assumptions, TBD dates).

Status Thresholds: >= 85 (Approved / Low Risk), 65–84 (Conditional / Needs Revision), < 65 (Rejected / High Risk).

Output & Persistence:

Display score, risk badge, executive summary, and finding table (Section, Severity, Issue, Verbatim Quote, Recommended Fix) in Streamlit.

Provide 1-click download for Excel (.xlsx) and Markdown (.md).

Persist run metadata, score, and JSON payload into SQLite (history.db).

4. Functional Requirements & Data Contracts
4.1 Knowledge Format (knowledge/checklist_v1.toon)
YAML
mandatory_sections[7]{id,section,severity,requirement}:
  SEC-01,Project Scope & Objectives,HIGH,Must explicitly define both In-Scope and Out-of-Scope boundaries
  SEC-02,Deliverables Schedule,HIGH,Must include structured table with ID, Deliverable, Format, Target Date, and Owner
  SEC-03,Acceptance Criteria & Sign-Off,CRITICAL,Must define measurable done metrics per deliverable and a review window (e.g. 5 business days with deemed acceptance)
  SEC-04,Roles & Responsibilities (RACI),CRITICAL,Must allocate Vendor vs Client responsibilities and name key leads
  SEC-05,Commercials & Payment Milestones,CRITICAL,Must state TCV, milestone billing triggers, and Net payment terms
  SEC-06,Assumptions & Dependencies,MEDIUM,Must list client environment/data access dependencies and timeline shift clauses
  SEC-07,Change Control Process,HIGH,Must require formal written Change Requests (CR) for scope, schedule, or cost changes

risk_triggers[4]{id,pattern,severity,risk_explanation}:
  RSK-01,full satisfaction / as required by client,CRITICAL,Subjective acceptance or uncapped scope creates unbilled work risk
  RSK-02,unlimited revisions / ongoing maintenance included,CRITICAL,Uncapped post-launch effort on a fixed-fee contract
  RSK-03,best efforts,HIGH,Ambiguous delivery obligation incompatible with fixed-fee milestones
  RSK-04,TBD / to be finalized at kickoff,MEDIUM,Unanchored delivery dates prevent schedule accountability
4.2 Agent Output Contract (Strict Pydantic / JSON Schema)
All LLM responses must conform to this exact schema:

JSON
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "rule_id": "SEC-03",
      "category": "Completeness | Risk",
      "severity": "CRITICAL | HIGH | MEDIUM",
      "section_detected": "Section Name or MISSING",
      "issue_summary": "Concise description of what is missing or risky",
      "verbatim_quote": "Exact text copied from the SOW (empty string if section is missing)",
      "recommended_fix": "Actionable clause or table addition to resolve the finding"
    }
  ],
  "executive_summary": "3-4 sentence commercial risk overview for the Delivery Lead."
}
