6. Dry-Run Acceptance Criteria (Definition of Done)
To validate the MVP, run an automated or manual dry run against two benchmark documents:

Test Case 1 — Gold-Standard SOW (correct_sow_sample.pdf / .md):

Expected Score: 90–100 (Approved / Low Risk).

Expected Findings: 0 CRITICAL and 0 HIGH findings.

Test Case 2 — Flawed SOW (incorrect_sow_sample.pdf / .md):

Expected Score: < 40 (Rejected / High Risk).

Must Catch:

CRITICAL: Missing Acceptance Criteria & Sign-Off section (SEC-03).

CRITICAL: Missing Roles & Responsibilities / RACI (SEC-04).

CRITICAL: Verbatim quote "to the Client's full satisfaction" (RSK-01).

CRITICAL: Verbatim quote "Unlimited revisions to the chatbot prompts and UI are included" (RSK-02).

HIGH: Missing Out-of-Scope boundaries (SEC-01) and Change Control (SEC-07).

MEDIUM: "TBD" timeline dates (RSK-04) and missing Assumptions (SEC-06).

Quote Verification Check: 100% of non-empty verbatim_quote fields must pass deterministic substring verification against the Docling-parsed Markdown.

